["19:47"]={
{"\0037:47 P.M.\004\nVance watched as the frigate got off a warning tracer, but to no effect. The Hind ignored it, as a stream of 57mm rockets from under the chopper’s stubby starboard wing flared down, while the radar-slaved machine gun beneath the nose opened fire.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover",true},
},
["19:48"]={
{"On the ride down in the elevator, Fenston was fascinated to see the low estimate for Caillebotte’s Street Sweepers. He had acquired the larger version for half that price from a client he had recently bankrupted. When the doors slid open, he walked quickly across to reception and signed himself out: \0037:48 P.M.\004","False Impression","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"\0037:48 P.M.\004\nThere are sounds of doors opening and closing, with whispered words that are like alien hisses. She senses she is in motion, on a bed that is gliding past powerful overhead lights.","Syndrome","Thomas Hoover",true},
},
["19:49"]={
{"When did you next see Dr. Wellesley?\n“At just \003eleven minutes to eight\004.”\n“Where?”\n“In the surgery.”\n“He came back there?”\n“Yes.”\n“How do you fix that precise time—eleven minutes to eight?”\n“Because he’d arranged to see a patient in Meadow Gate at ten minutes to eight. I glanced at the clock as he came in, saw what time it was, and reminded him of the appointment.”","In the Mayor’s Parlour","J.S. Fletcher",true},
{"\003Eleven minutes to eight\004.\n“You’re always right; there must be a clock in your head.”\n“I can’t be wrong, tonight. I’ll be able to tell you one second before they blast off. Look! The ten-minute warning!”","The End of the Beginning","Ray Bradbury",true},
},
["19:50"]={
{"Everything was arranged for them. A real limousine came at \003ten minutes to eight\004 and took them to the theater. It drew up under the marquee at exactly the right time, after the big stars and the director and the author and the governor and the mayor and some less important stars.","A Late Encounter with the Enemy","Flannery O’Connor",true},
{"The hands of the clock in the middle of the wall were pointing to \003ten minutes to eight\004. The cafe closed at eight.","Before the Coffee Gets Cold: Tales from the Cafe","Toshikazu Kawaguchi",true},
{"At \003ten to eight\004, he strolled downstairs, to make sure that Signora Buffi was not pottering around in the hall and that her door was not open, and to make sure there really was no one in Freddie’s car","The Talented Mr. Ripley","Patricia Highsmith",true},
},
["19:51"]={
{"Annie somehow managed to shower and change into a cocktail dress, while Fletcher paced around the room looking at his watch every few moments. He opened the cab door for his wife at \0037:51\004.","Sons of Fortune","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"The plane swung around onto the take-off runway at \0037:51\004, its jets revving before it moved slowly forward, then gathered speed. The wheels left the ground at 7:53.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"He waited until \003nearly eight\004, because around seven there were always more people coming in and out of the house than at other times. At ten to eight, he strolled downstairs, to make sure that Signora Buffi was not pottering around in the hall and that her door was not open, and to make sure there really was no one in Freddie’s car, though he had gone down in the middle of the afternoon to look at the car and see if it was Freddie’s.","The Talented Mr. Ripley","Patricia Highsmith",true},
},
["19:52"]={
{"\0037:52 P.M.\004\nVance pulled himself across the planking and stretched for a box of gear stowed beneath the stern platform. In it was a constant traveling companion: his chrome-handled 9mm Walther. Although the concept of downing a Hind gunship with small-arms fire had been tested in Afghanistan and found wanting, he was so angry his better judgment was not fully in play.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover",true},
},
